](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/82766) )

Tries to insert a key-value pair into the map, and returns a mutable reference
to the value in the entry.

If the map already had this key present, nothing is updated, and an error
containing the occupied entry and the value is returned.

#####  Â§  Examples

Basic usage:



    #![feature(map_try_insert)]

    use std::collections::HashMap;

    let mut map = HashMap::new();
    assert_eq!(map.try_insert(37, "a").unwrap(), &"a");

    let err = map.try_insert(37, "b").unwrap_err();
    assert_eq!(err.entry.key(), &37);
    assert_eq!(err.entry.get(), &"a");
    assert_eq!(err.value, "b");

