How to make MudSelect show text of selected option instead of value?

```
<MudSelect MultiSelection="true" @bind-SelectedValues="ViewModel.Model.GlobalSalaryAccessUserIds">
                @foreach (var salaryAccessUser in ViewModel.GlobalSalaryAccessUsers)
                {
                    <MudSelectItem Value="@salaryAccessUser.Id">@GenerateSalaryAccessUserDisplayString(salaryAccessUser)</MudSelectItem>
                }
            </MudSelect>
```

Now instead of string which generates in `GenerateSalaryAccessUserDisplayString` it shows a value of the option, which is id, when I've selected a few of them . How can I change it to show the generated string?

gold_answer:
Found the answer. You can use ` ToStringFunc ` attribute of ` MudSelect ` .

In your code behind you have to declare a ` Func<'your option value
type',string> ` and apply it to ` ToStringFunc ` .

My case:



    <MudSelect MultiSelection="true" @bind-SelectedValues="ViewModel.Model.GlobalSalaryAccessUserIds" Variant="Variant.Outlined" Label="Manager" ToStringFunc="ToStringConverter">
                        @foreach (var salaryAccessUser in ViewModel.GlobalSalaryAccessUsers)
                        {
                            <MudSelectItem Value="@(salaryAccessUser.Id)">@GenerateSalaryAccessUserDisplayString(salaryAccessUser)</MudSelectItem>
                        }
                    </MudSelect>

    // ------------ Code behind ------------------
    protected Func<int, string> ToStringConverter;

    // Have to initialize it separately
    protected override Task OnInitializedComponentAsync()
    {
        ToStringConverter = GenerateSalaryAccessUserDisplayString;

        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private string GenerateSalaryAccessUserDisplayString(int salaryAccessUserId)
        {
            var salaryAccessUser = ViewModel.GlobalSalaryAccessUsers.FirstOrDefault(u => u.Id == salaryAccessUserId);

            return $"{salaryAccessUser.FirstName} {salaryAccessUser.LastName}";
        }

